Subject: [PATCH 2/2] diag(build): name the composition of the P4 diagnostic in
 BuildConfig

82c1af9 (installed and validated on the fixture on 16/11) plus P4 (e57dd89 on
research/p0-peaks-20261116, cherry-picked unchanged). Still a diagnostic build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
index d2c05a8..6fa79ce 100644
--- a/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
+++ b/05_Firmware/MATDOG_Controller/src/config/BuildConfig.h
@@ -163,6 +163,9 @@ constexpr const char* kFirmwareDescription = "Embedded Motion & Robot Control Fi
 //   plus the accepted offset), P3a (bit-identical ViaPlan::plan), P3b (plan
 //   release keeps the probe) and D3 (last release lost with Motion idle, the
 //   @MOTION TIMING dump duration, the register-85 pass duration).
+// P4 diagnostic (composed 2026-11-16 on 82c1af9, validated on the chip the same
+//   day): plus P4, every attenuated release keeps the probe when its scale does
+//   not exceed the projection (one solve instead of two). Still diagnostic.
 constexpr const char* kFirmwareVersion = "1.0.2-dev.8"; // P0 diagnostic build only; not an operational candidate
 constexpr const char* kBoardName       = "YD-ESP32-S3 N16R8";
 constexpr const char* kBuildId         = MATDOG_BUILD_ID;
